{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"3768 plan-review: BLOCK with 9 findings, all fair — I wrote the Approach as 'candidate, not a decision' and the gate correctly refuses a plan that defers its primary design decision. NEW VERIFIED FINDING from the review: completion.py:332 carries the SAME equality-test inversion as verify.py:269, on a separate path, so THREE gates lose their verifier downgrade on a non-default model (plan-review, code-review, completion) — my plan named only two. Also note completion.py pins temperature=0 for greedy decoding right below that line (bug e458), the same determinism property 1903 showed is silently lost on opus-4-8. 3768 is NOT claimable until its six deferred design decisions are made; it is also the highest-leverage ticket (blocks both S6 and S8), so the design pass IS the critical path. Closed 3a98 and 281f (both --class plan_defect) this iteration; a574 plan-review PASSED and is claimable."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785465313650107001,"uuid":"5e9a28e7-16ec-4b73-8476-ad4c2bec337a"}